"q": "<p>An obiect is thrown upward into the air 10 meters above the ground. The figure above shows the initiaposition of the object and the position at a later time. At time t seconds after the object is thrown upwardthe horizontal distance from the initial position is given by x(t) meters, and the vertical distance from the ground is given by y(t) meters, where <span class=\"tex\">{\\frac{d x}{d t}}=1.4</span> and <span class=\"tex\">{\\frac{d y}{d t}}=4.2-9.8t</span>,for t <span class=\"tex\">\\ge</span> 0 .Find the angle <span class=\"tex\">\\theta</span>, 0 &lt; <span class=\"tex\">\\theta</span> &lt; <span class=\"tex\">\\pi</span>/2 , between the path of the object and the ground at the instance the objecthit the ground. Options: A. <span class=\"tex\">\\theta</span> = 0.524; B. <span class=\"tex\">\\theta</span> = 1.047; C. <span class=\"tex\">\\theta</span> = 1.475; D. <span class=\"tex\">\\theta</span> = 1.570.</p>",
"a": "<div class=\"texd\">y(t)=10+4.2t-4.9t^2</div><p>The object hits the ground when <span class=\"tex\">y(t)=0</span>:</p><div class=\"texd\">4.9t^2-4.2t-10=0</div><div class=\"texd\">t\\approx 1.92</div><p>At that time,</p><div class=\"texd\">\\frac{dy}{dt}=4.2-9.8t\\approx -14.616</div><p>and</p><div class=\"texd\">\\frac{dx}{dt}=1.4</div><p>So the slope of the path is</p><div class=\"texd\">\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{dy/dt}{dx/dt}\\approx \\frac{-14.616}{1.4}=-10.44</div><p>The angle with the ground is</p><div class=\"texd\">\\theta=\\tan^{-1}(10.44)\\approx 1.475</div><p><b>Answer: C. <span class=\"tex\">\\theta=1.475</span></b></p>",
